er.\",\"reason\":\"Not-a-bug point added to a8; capacity point carried by a9.\"},{\"segment\":\"b11\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"Callers that retry at once are the largest single reason the cap is there at all.\",\"reason\":\"Same point; base wording kept.\"},{\"segment\":\"b13\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"The refusal carries a Retry-After header.\",\"reason\":\"Header name; base wording kept.\"},{\"segment\":\"b14\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"Its value is a whole number of seconds to wait, and it is present on every refusal the gateway sends.\",\"reason\":\"Header value merged with a13; presence fact retained.\"},{\"segment\":\"b15\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"Waiting that long and then continuing is the whole of the contract — a client that does it needs nothing else from this document, which is the outcome it was written for, however unlikely that makes it to be read at all.\",\"reason\":\"Contract sentence merged with a14; closing remark retained.\"},{\"segment\":\"b16\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely, so waiting longer than the header asks earns a caller no credit at all.\",\"reason\":\"Same point; base wording kept.\"},{\"segment\":\"b17\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"The body of the refusal is JSON, and it names what the gateway calls the “window” it counted in. It names the cap and the tier as well, all as plain fields.\",\"reason\":\"Body description carried by a16 and the extended a17.\"},{\"segment\":\"b18\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"None of those fields is a substitute for the header, and a caller that parses the body to compute its own wait is doing the same arithmetic twice, in code whose only possible future is to disagree with the gateway it is talking to.\",\"reason\":\"Body-parsing sentence merged with a18.\"},{\"segment\":\"b19\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"The body is there so that a human reading a log afterwards can see why the request was refused — nothing in it is meant for the retry loop.\",\"reason\":\"Same point; base wording is fuller.\"},{\"segment\":\"b20\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"## How to retry well\",\"reason\":\"Section heading: base heading kept.\"},{\"segment\":\"b21\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"Four rules, given in the order they should be applied.\",\"reason\":\"Same statement; base wording kept.\"},{\"segment\":\"b22\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"1. Honour the header, every time. The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have, and it does the same on the 503 path, even though the cause of the refusal there is an entirely different one. A wait derived on the client side is a guess about a counter it cannot see.\",\"reason\":\"Rule 1: base wording kept; own-wait point carried by a24.\"},{\"segment\":\"b23\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have, and it does the same on the 503 path, even though the cause of the refusal there is an entirely different one.\",\"reason\":\"Same rationale; carried in the combined sentence.\"},{\"segment\":\"b24\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have, and it does the same on the 503 path, even though the cause of the refusal there is an entirely different one.\",\"reason\":\"503 rule merged into the rule 1 rationale sentence.\"},{\"segment\":\"b25\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"A wait derived on the client side is a guess about a counter it cannot see.\",\"reason\":\"Same point; base wording kept.\"},{\"segment\":\"b26\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"There is no case at all where a guess is the better of the two.\",